      "description": "Watch Sporting CP vs Guimaraes highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 14, 2026. On 2026-08-14 , Sporting CP and Vitoria de Guimaraes locked horns in a Primeira Liga fixture that delivered pure drama. The encounter shifted from a one-sided masterclass to a nail-biting finish as both sides displayed incredible fighting spirit. Dominant Start for the Lions Sporting CP wasted no time establishing control on their home turf. In the 9th minute, Flavio Goncalves clinical right-footed strike broke the deadlock following an assist from Fotis Ioannidis . The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and by the 22nd minute, Fotis Ioannidis turned scorer, finding the net with his left foot after being set up by Geny Catamo . The first half reached a crescendo in the 41st minute when Sergi Altimira unleashed a brilliant strike from outside the penalty area. Although a VAR check briefly paused the celebrations, the goal stood, giving Sporting CP what looked like an insurmountable three-goal lead heading into the break. Guimaraes' Spirited Fightback The complexion of the match changed drastically in the second half. Vitoria de Guimaraes refused to go down quietly and struck twice in quick succession. In the 66th minute, Samu finished with his left foot to pull one back. Just two minutes later, Alioune Ndoye rose highest to head home a cross from Tony Strata , suddenly bringing the score to 3-2 and silence to the home crowd. The final stages were frantic and ill-disciplined as tension boiled over. Yellow cards were brandished to Eduardo Quaresma and Goncalo Inacio for dissent, while Gustavo Silva saw red for a rough challenge. Despite the late pressure and a missed chance by Gustavo Silva in stoppage time, Sporting CP managed to weather the storm and secure a hard-fought victory."
